{title: As I Rise To Walk With Him}
{artist: Larry Holder / Elton Smith}
{time: 4/4}
{key: D}
{tempo: 103}

>Lyrics

Introduction

Verse 1

Except a seed be returned to the earth,

There to die to itself,

And yet to find its rebirth,

So I now testify

I am born from above,

Trusting in the Savior's love!

Chorus

As I die (as I die) to my sin (to my sin)

I am raised unto life everlasting with Him.

Praise the Lord for His love

Shining down from above

As I rise to walk with Him.

Verse 2

No more a slave to the sin that I knew,

For the Lord's cleansing power

Now has made all things new.

Washed away is the old

By the blood of the Lamb;

By His grace alone I stand!

(Repeat Chorus)

As I die (as I die) to my sin (to my sin)

I am raised unto life everlasting with Him.

Praise the Lord for His love

Shining down from above

As I rise to walk with Him.

(Banjo and fiddle solo)

(Repeat Chorus)

As I die (as I die) to my sin (to my sin)

I am raised unto life everlasting with Him.

Praise the Lord for His love

Shining down from above

As I rise to walk with Him.
